<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar inflows at $188.4 mln Oct 8.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar inflows at $188.4 mln Oct 8.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $188.4 million surplus on October 8 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the central bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON OCTOBER 8</p>
<p>Exports: $193.2 million</p>
<p>Imports: $154.1 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $280.6 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $131.3 million</p>
<p>Surplus: $188.4 million</p>
<p>OCTOBER DOLLAR FLOWS UP TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $950 million</p>
<p>Imports: $775 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $1.379 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $804 million</p>
<p>Net surplus: $750 million</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55-11-2324411</p>
